    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Trea Turner** (76.35) and **Kyle Schwarber** (75.20), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against the hittable Roki Sasaki (5.11 xERA). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.81) represents our premier stolen base threat today; his efficiency is bolstered by the leadoff spot and a strong platoon advantage against Kyle Leahy. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** (72.26) remains a must-start despite a modest park factor, as his elite 0.424 xwOBA provides the highest offensive ceiling in the lineup. **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) and **Christian Yelich** (69.64) round out our top-tier plays, both thriving on clear platoon advantages and high-leverage order positions.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a score of 46.96. While **Chase Meidroth** offered decent positional flexibility, he was ultimately benched due to the difficulty of facing Framber Valdez and a suboptimal spot in the order. We are also monitoring the status of **Caleb Durbin**, whose proximity to the starting threshold (39.98) makes him our primary depth option should late-scratch reports surface. Note that **Zac Veen** and **Hyeseong Kim** remain in the minors and are currently unavailable for selection. Managers should remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the roster, as any defensive shift\u2014specifically for **Dillon Dingler** or **Casey Schmitt**\u2014could impact the order-based bonuses currently driving their strong efficiency scores.",
